{{mcn|date=October 2024}}
[[File:Labeling of new specimens. Institute of Systematics and Evolution of Animals Polish Academy of Sciences in Cracov.jpg|thumb|The labeling of a specimen after its taxonomic identity has been determined.]]
In biology, '''determination''' is the process of matching a specimen or sample of an organism to a known [[taxon]], for example identifying a plant as belonging to a particular [[species]]. Expert taxonomists may perform this task, but structures created by taxonomists are sometimes used by non-specialists. Modern tools include [[single-access key|single]] or [[multi-access key|multi-access]] [[identification key]]s, which can be printed or computer-assisted.

